   "body": "### Capture result\n\nPR #737 holds corpus ids `R716a`-`R716e`, captured 2026-11-10 with user1 and without cookies, read-only.\n\n- A one-to-one MP row's link `/profilebdd.php?config=hfr.inc&pseudo=<pseudo>` answers one `301` to a relative `/hfr/profil-<id>.htm`. The answer is the same logged in and without cookies, with an empty body and no cookie set. The target is the public profile page that `UserProfileParser` reads: logged in it adds an \"Ajouter <pseudo> à votre liste de contacts\" row (`R716b`), and logged out it is `R56a`.\n- An unknown pseudo gets a `301` to `/hfr/profil-.htm` (empty id), which answers the web server's `404 Not Found` page (`R716d`, `R716e`).\n- **What this changes:** #714 can take the member id from the `Location` of a single non-followed request, then read the avatar from the profile page or from the `mesdiscussions-<id>` image. An empty id means there is no such member. Facts are in HFR-PROTOCOL §6c \"#714 — `profilebdd.php` redirect\". No merged lot or spec must change, so no follow-up issue.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
